ostrya (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Store the composefs image of a commit as a .cfs object. commit
    --generate-composefs stores the image. Add composefs-image. Prune
    removes the image with its commit, and fsck checks each image.
  * Carry the composefs image in pull, push, send, serve, and static
    deltas.
  * Write each ref into the root summary, and write the summary of the
    anonymous item under extensions/ostrya/summary/.
  * Add summary -c/--client-groups.
  * State archive-z2 in each served summary.
  * Keep the summary of the anonymous item served after a mirror pull.
  * Start a plain HTTP serve next to an HTTPS serve of one repository.
  * Add the template unit ostrya-serve@.service and the sysusers.d file of
    the user ostrya. Build ostrya-mountd from its own source package.

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:29:56 +0200

ostrya (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Control the access to a served repository with client groups in the
    repository config. The receive policy groups are removed.
  * Take the settings of ostrya serve from the [ex-ostrya server] group.
  * Identify a client of ostrya serve by a client certificate, and serve
    behind a trusted proxy or with the PROXY protocol.
  * Rename the serve option --client-ca to --tls-client-ca.
  * Push into collection namespaces, and list and pull collection refs.
  * Build a server commit on the server for push --onto and push-tree.
  * Write and serve a summary for each auth item. Add summary --auth-group.
  * Add commit --tag.
  * Accept named GC anchors in prune, and refuse a bad value of a GC anchor
    key in commit.
  * Add the man pages ostrya-repo(5) and ostrya-config(1).

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:56:29 +0200

ostrya (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install the man pages of the ostrya command.
  * Give each help item a short line for -h and a long text for --help.
  * Wrap the --help text to the width of the terminal.

